 R←Test_Misc_011(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;C;ref;res
⍝ Quits the project selection that <EstablishProject> offers when nothing was specified.
⍝ <U.SelectProject> tested for that with "¯1≡i::'' ''" - a double colon, which makes it an ERROR
⍝ GUARD rather than a condition. Quitting therefore fell through to l[¯1;] and gave an INDEX
⍝ ERROR, while a normal selection installed a catch-all that swallowed any later error.
⍝ Uses the documented ∆OPEN_PROJECTS seam, so no project is opened or closed.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 ref←''

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 ref←⎕SE.APLGit2.##.UC.GetRefToAPLGit2 ⍬        ⍝ Whatever the user commands execute
 ref.##.U.∆OPEN_PROJECTS←2 2⍴'#.Fake1'tempDir'#.Fake2'tempDir
 C←∆GetRefToCommTools
 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'SelectPrjForAPLGIT2@' 'q'   ⍝ "q" = quit

 res←G.EstablishProject''
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠≢res
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∧/0=≢¨res                       ⍝ Two empty vectors, no INDEX ERROR

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :Trap 0 ⋄ {}ref.##.U.⎕EX'∆OPEN_PROJECTS' ⋄ :EndTrap
 C.Cleanup
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
